From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GIMPhoto scripts <gimphoto@localhost>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:42:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Clipping masks: Create / Release Clipping Mask, Alt+click
 between layers

Photoshop's clipping masks: a layer clipped to the layer below it (its base)
shows only where the base has pixels. Several layers can be clipped to one
base; each keeps its own mode, opacity and mask; the base's mode, opacity and
mask apply to the whole run; clipped layers are drawn indented with a bent
arrow in the Layers panel.

- app/core/gimplayer.[ch]: a `clipped` flag (gimp_layer_set_clipped, with
  undo; gimp_layer_can_be_clipped: not the bottom layer of a group), the
  "clipped-changed" signal, and the "gimphoto-clipped" parasite mirroring
  the flag so plug-ins (the PSD loader and exporter) and the XCF carry it
  without a PDB procedure. A clipped layer's effective composite mode is
  Clip to backdrop. _gimp_layer_set_clip_base wires a base's node: its own
  pixels (Normal over nothing, with its mask) leave through a "clip-base"
  output, and a "clip-result" input takes the place of its pixels at its
  mode node; the mask signals re-wire it after GIMP's mask code.
- app/core/gimplayerstack.c: whenever the stack or a clipping changes,
  the chain is rewired: the base's clip-base feeds the first clipped layer,
  each clipped layer the next, the last one the base's clip-result, and the
  unclipped chain skips the clipped layers. A clipped layer with no base
  (bottom, or its base hidden) shows as an ordinary layer. A layer added
  with the parasite becomes clipped. gimpfilterstack.[ch]: a graph_built
  hook so the stack rewires the graph GimpFilterStack builds.
- app/core/gimpimage-merge.c: merging reads the composite at the base of
  a clipped top layer. Undo: GIMP_UNDO_LAYER_CLIPPED in GimpLayerPropUndo.
- app/actions, menus: Layer > Create / Release Clipping Mask (one toggle,
  the label follows the first selected layer), also in the Layers panel's
  menu; Ctrl+Alt+G in the keymap, reaching existing profiles through a
  shortcut move from "-" (app/menus/menus.c: a shortcut new to GIMPhoto).
- app/widgets/gimpcontainertreeview.[ch]: a gap_clicked class hook for
  Alt+click within 4 px of the line between two rows;
  gimplayertreeview.c implements it (clip or release the upper layer) and
  shows the gimphoto-clipping-mask icon before a clipped layer's
  thumbnail, which indents it.
- plug-ins/file-psd: clipped PSD layers load as clipped layers (the
  parasite) instead of GIMP's "Group added by GIMP" with Clip to backdrop;
  the exporter writes the clipping byte for them.

Test: two layers, Alt+click the line between them or Ctrl+Alt+G on the
upper one; it shows only inside the lower one; hide the base and the
clipped layer vanishes; drag the base to the bottom... ; Flatten and Merge
Down bake it; a PSD from Photoshop with clipped layers opens clipped and
exports clipped; the XCF reopens clipped.

